HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The functions sslleeeepp() and wwaakkeeuupp() were present in Version 1 AT&T UNIX.
     They were probably also present in the preceding PDP-7 version of UNIX.
     They were the basic process synchronization model.

     The ttsslleeeepp() function appeared in 4.4BSD and added the parameters _w_m_e_s_g
     and _t_i_m_o.  The sslleeeepp() function was removed in FreeBSD 2.2.  The
     wwaakkeeuupp__oonnee() function appeared in FreeBSD 2.2.  The mmsslleeeepp() function ap‐
     peared in FreeBSD 5.0, and the mmsslleeeepp__ssppiinn() function appeared in
     FreeBSD 6.2.  The ppaauussee() function appeared in FreeBSD 7.0.  The
     ppaauussee__ssiigg() function appeared in FreeBSD 12.0.

